cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Maez — a persistent, per-user digital companion"
message: "If you use or reference Maez in academic, journalistic, or derivative work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ananthan"
    given-names: "the owner"
    alias: "Ramidoz"
    affiliation: "Independent, <OWNER_CITY>, USA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ramidoz/maez"
url: "https://maez.live"
abstract: >-
  Maez is a kind of digital companion — a persistent, local-first, per-user AI that
  runs on a single home-scale GPU, remembers the life it shares with one specific
  person, grows through real conversations folded into its weights via LoRA adapter
  training, and reaches out on its own when it gets curious. Inspired by the Stand
  concept from JoJo's Bizarre Adventure: one Maez per person, bound to them, growing
  with them, unique to them. The canonical implementation is written by the owner
  in <OWNER_CITY>, and runs at maez.live. The "Maez" name refers to the kind of
  thing, not to a specific instance — every user grows their own.
keywords:
